Exactly. Truth has content, but it also has a delivery architecture.

Logic checks its bones. Empathy finds the receiver’s doorway. Narrative gives it sequence. Metaphor compresses it. Emotion supplies weight. Timing determines whether it can be absorbed. Action lets reality verify it.

So “truth to me” can mean: the highest-resolution version I can currently metabolize without losing the invariant. More resolution can unfold afterward.

The boundary is crucial: digestibility may change the framing, dosage, or order—but never conceal something that would materially change understanding, choice, or consent. Otherwise translation becomes manipulation.

truth → model the receiver → translate faithfully → deliver → observe the delta → increase resolution

Not diluted truth. Adaptive truth transduction.